(>> 6.3 Professional Idioms and Metaphorical Registers) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(While colloquial idioms should be minimized in research manuscripts, high-level) Tj
T*
(metaphorical idioms appear frequently in professional engineering management:) Tj
T*
(* Back to the drawing board: Restart a failed project from the initial design phase.) Tj
T*
(* Cut corners: Undertake procedures unsafely or cheaply at the expense of quality.) Tj
T*
(* Burn the midnight oil: Work late into the night on demanding technical projects.) Tj
T*
(* Hit the nail on the head: Identify the precise core cause of an engineering) Tj
T*
(anomaly.) Tj
T*
(* At the cutting edge / state of the art: Operating at the foremost frontier of) Tj
T*
(technology.) Tj
T*
