([EXERCISE 1: Formal Latinate Replacement of Informal Phrasal Verbs]) Tj
T*
(Problem: Replace the informal phrasal verbs in the following sentences with precise,) Tj
T*
(single-word formal academic equivalents:) Tj
T*
(Sentence 1: "The research team carried out [ _________ ] the genetic sequencing) Tj
T*
(protocol.") Tj
T*
(- Formal Replacement: CONDUCTED / EXECUTED / PERFORMED.) Tj
T*
(Sentence 2: "The organic contaminants broke down [ _________ ] within forty-eight) Tj
T*
(hours.") Tj
T*
(- Formal Replacement: DECOMPOSED / DEGRADED.) Tj
T*
(Sentence 3: "The engineering committee will look into [ _________ ] the pump failure.") Tj
T*
(- Formal Replacement: INVESTIGATE / EXAMINE.) Tj
T*
(Sentence 4: "The principal investigator pointed out [ _________ ] the discrepancy in the) Tj
T*
(absorbance values.") Tj
T*
(- Formal Replacement: INDICATED / HIGHLIGHTED.) Tj
T*
(Sentence 5: "We must figure out [ _________ ] the mechanism governing membrane) Tj
T*
(transport.") Tj
T*
(- Formal Replacement: ELUCIDATE / DETERMINE / DEDUCE.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([EXERCISE 2: Homophone and Confused Word Disambiguation Drill]) Tj
T*
(Problem: Select the correct lexical item in each of the following engineering sentences:) Tj
T*
(Sentence 1: "The addition of heavy metal ions adversely \(affected / effected\) cell) Tj
T*
(viability.") Tj
T*
(- Solution: AFFECTED. \(Verb meaning 'influenced'\).) Tj
T*
(Sentence 2: "The spectrophotometer works on the fundamental \(principal / principle\) of) Tj
