([EXERCISE 3: Precision Academic Sentence Rewriting]) Tj
T*
(Problem: Eliminate wordiness, colloquialisms, and redundant phrasing in the following) Tj
T*
(excerpt:) Tj
T*
(Wordy Draft: "At this point in time, it is really totally obvious that the reason why) Tj
T*
(the reaction failed was because of the fact that the technician didn't bother to check) Tj
T*
(the temperature.") Tj
T*
(Concise Academic Revision: "The reaction failed because the technician did not verify) Tj
T*
(the operating temperature.") Tj
T*
(Linguistic Analysis:) Tj
T*
(- 'At this point in time' -> Eliminated \(redundant fluff\).) Tj
T*
(- 'really totally obvious' -> Eliminated \(colloquial intensifiers\).) Tj
T*
(- 'the reason why ... was because of the fact that' -> Reduced to a single clean) Tj
T*
(conjunction: 'because'.) Tj
T*
(- 'didn't bother to check' -> Upgraded to professional diction: 'did not verify'.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([EXERCISE 4: Contextual Vocabulary Synthesis in Biotechnology Context]) Tj
T*
(Problem: Match each technical definition with its correct academic term \(Elucidate,) Tj
T*
(Inhibit, Titrate, Lyophilize, Precipitate\):) Tj
T*
(1. To determine the concentration of a dissolved substance by adding measured volumes of) Tj
T*
(a standardized reagent: TITRATE.) Tj
T*
(2. To freeze-dry a biological sample under high vacuum to preserve protein stability:) Tj
T*
(LYOPHILIZE.) Tj
T*
(3. To make lucid, clear, or explain a complex biochemical pathway: ELUCIDATE.) Tj
T*
(4. To hinder, restrain, or suppress an enzymatic reaction: INHIBIT.) Tj
T*
(5. To separate an insoluble solid substance from a solution: PRECIPITATE.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
